From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: bb's cloud plugins are not shipped

1ma does not ship bb's cloud services, which send data to getbb.app, until
1ma runs its own. The bb-account, bb-ai, connect and connect-next plugins
stay in BUNDLED_PLUGINS, because bb's catalog generator needs an entry for
each item there, but SHIPPED_PLUGINS and the bundled registrations leave
them out. They are not built into the app, not installed, and not listed in
the store (the bundled marketplace filters by registration names).

The desktop Server menu offered "Sign in to bb Connect" whenever there was
no saved credential, even when the local server said the connect plugin was
disabled or not installed. A 404 "unknown plugin" answer now maps to
"plugin-disabled", and that reason wins over "no-credential", so the menu
shows no sign-in item.

The AI services text and search keyword no longer mention bb cloud.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
